{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'not-used|deferred|required.*producer' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review* | head -35; rg -n 'tool.*evidence|Tool.*Evidence' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attestation* | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:87:const briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:91:// precondition is the completion of the review is answered deferred, the component scoping of\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:102:\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1956:\t\tcase \"not-used\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1960:\t\t\t\t// The one required tool that may be not-used is the one the\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1964:\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"required review tool \"+label+\" has no registered producer and still needs a not-used rationale\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1966:\t\t\t\twarnings = append(warnings, \"recommended review tool \"+label+\" lacks not-used rationale\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1968:\t\tcase \"deferred\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1970:\t\t\t\tmessage := \"review tool \" + label + \" has invalid deferred disposition\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1981:\t\t\t!(tool.ProducerCoverage == \"none\" && disposition.Disposition == \"not-used\" && disposition.Rationale != \"\") {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go:559:\t\t\ttools.WriteString(\"- \" + tool.ID + \" [deferred] rationale:post-review-gate\\n\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go:563:\t\t\ttools.WriteString(\"- \" + tool.ID + \" [not-used]\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go:615:\tmissingRecommendedBody := strings.Replace(body, \"- assess-discover [not-used] component:api rationale:not-needed\\n\", \"\", 1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go:140:\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition, disposition.Rationale = \"deferred\", \"post-review gate\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go:142:\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition, disposition.Rationale = \"not-used\", \"not needed for fixture\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go:152:\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition, disposition.Rationale = \"not-used\", \"the fixture seals no evidence of a class this tool reports\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go:956:\t\tTools: []ReviewToolDisposition{{ID: \"validate\", Disposition: \"deferred\", Rationale: \"no declared delivery target\"}},\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go:964:\tif !strings.Contains(strings.Join(blockers, \" \"), \"review tool validate has invalid deferred disposition\") {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go:965:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"declared target allowed deferred validation: %+v\", blockers)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go:1201:\t\t\trequested+\" from a component the validation matrix declares runs no check; record it not-used with the reason, or register a check for that component\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:2889:\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"deferred\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:2896:\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"not-used\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:2899:\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"not-used\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:2930:\t\t\t\t// `deferred`, not `not-used`: a required tool recorded not-used\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:2934:\t\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"deferred\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_